WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.324 --> 00:00:17.372
"Wow," Ally thought.

2
00:00:18.073 --> 00:00:20.234
"Ray is nervous about this gala."

3
00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:26.438
"The League of Rocket Scientists read about the diner in Gourmet Greta's column," Ray said.

4
00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:30.300
"They love our space theme, but they want a special menu for their dinner.

5
00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:34.314
I was thinking of serving grilled salmon, but what would I call it?"

6
00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:42.039
"I bet Ally can think of some out-of-this-world ideas," Mateo said.

7
00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:43.821
"Solar Salmon!"

8
00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:45.021
Ally suggested.

9
00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:50.125
"Hey, Ray," Randy, the assistant cook, called from Ray's office.

10
00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:51.926
"You've got a phone call."

11
00:00:51.946 --> 00:00:54.928
"Coming!" Ray hurried to his office.

12
00:00:54.948 --> 00:00:59.551
"Ally, what are some of the best meals in the galaxy?"

13
00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:00.712
Mateo asked.

14
00:01:01.472 --> 00:01:08.955
"Hmm I'd say Formarian Frittata and Ally trailed off when she spotted the new waiter, Barry, outside, taking

15
00:01:09.016 --> 00:01:09.956
pictures of the diner.

16
00:01:11.657 --> 00:01:16.379
Ally had learned a lot about humans, but Barry's behavior was still mysterious to her at times.

17
00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:19.040
"What's he taking pictures of?"

18
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:23.902
Mateo turned to look, but as soon as Barry saw them looking, he put his phone away.

19
00:01:24.423 --> 00:01:27.284
Then he rushed inside and sat down at the counter next to Phil.

20
00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:32.816
Mateo shrugged.

21
00:01:32.836 --> 00:01:36.497
"Why does Barry do a lot of the things he does?"

22
00:01:37.578 --> 00:01:42.399
Ally quickly read Barry's mind, but as usual, he was thinking about ways to make his father proud.

23
00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:49.561
"Back to ideas for Ray," Ally said.

24
00:01:49.581 --> 00:01:53.242
"Formarian Frittata would make a great appetizer.

25
00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:58.503
And Meltron Moon Pies could be a fun dessert, oh, and—" "That was the league's secretary on the

26
00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:00.104
phone." Ray hurried over.

27
00:02:01.016 --> 00:02:03.417
"They want to make sure that you work at the gala, Ally.

28
00:02:03.878 --> 00:02:04.918
They want to see your tricks."

29
00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.020
"Sure!" Ally said brightly.

30
00:02:10.261 --> 00:02:11.782
But inside she was nervous.

31
00:02:11.802 --> 00:02:15.284
"Do these rocket scientists want to be entertained?"

32
00:02:15.724 --> 00:02:16.144
she thought.

33
00:02:16.164 --> 00:02:18.446
"Or have they heard rumors about me?

34
00:02:18.986 --> 00:02:20.067
I'd better be careful."

35
00:02:20.087 --> 00:02:22.828
"Tricks? Gala?"

36
00:02:23.388 --> 00:02:24.469
Barry's ears perked up.

37
00:02:24.489 --> 00:02:27.491
"Can I work too, Ray?

38
00:02:27.611 --> 00:02:29.572
Please?" Ray nodded.

39
00:02:30.384 --> 00:02:31.505
"I need everyone that night."

40
00:02:32.365 --> 00:02:34.286
He gathered up the cookbooks and went to the kitchen.

41
00:02:38.187 --> 00:02:39.168
Barry looked at Ally.

42
00:02:39.848 --> 00:02:41.389
"Now you'll have to teach me your tricks."

43
00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:43.350
Ally sighed.

44
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:48.952
"Fine. We can begin tomorrow when we're both working."

45
00:02:48.972 --> 00:02:54.174
"Yes!" Barry pumped his arm in triumph and went back to sit with Phil.

46
00:02:57.415 --> 00:02:58.596
Mateo shot her a look.

47
00:02:59.532 --> 00:03:02.274
"You can't teach him how to levitate a plate, can you?"

48
00:03:02.674 --> 00:03:03.214
he whispered.

49
00:03:07.557 --> 00:03:09.177
course not," Ally said.

50
00:03:09.197 --> 00:03:14.080
"But he keeps asking me to teach him tricks, and I can't keep making excuses.

51
00:03:15.281 --> 00:03:17.602
That might make him even more suspicious of me.

52
00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:19.003
Don't worry."

53
00:03:19.423 --> 00:03:20.904
She glanced at the bag of coils.

54
00:03:20.924 --> 00:03:22.705
"I have a plan."

55
00:03:23.886 --> 00:03:25.947
Mateo nodded, but he still looked worried.

56
00:03:25.967 --> 00:03:27.588
"I hope it works.

57
00:03:29.032 --> 00:03:31.453
I'm meeting Bethany for a bike ride in the park.

58
00:03:32.113 --> 00:03:32.713
See you later."

59
00:03:35.174 --> 00:03:39.155
After Ally started her shift, one of her first customers was a woman at the counter.

60
00:03:42.336 --> 00:03:45.256
She barely looked up from her phone when Ally came to take her order.

61
00:03:45.276 --> 00:03:49.778
"I'll have five gallons of silver paint, please," the woman said.

62
00:03:49.798 --> 00:03:54.059
"We only serve yellow paint here," Ally joked.

63
00:03:54.999 --> 00:03:56.239
The woman looked up and laughed.

64
00:03:59.044 --> 00:04:01.987
"Sorry! I'm so distracted by my work."

65
00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:05.609
"Why do you need silver paint?"

66
00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:06.630
Ally asked.

67
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:14.297
"I've been commissioned by the Sandville Arts Board to create sculptures from objects found or seen around town.

68
00:04:16.058 --> 00:04:18.380
I need silver paint to finish a sculpture."

69
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:24.045
"I've seen a few of your sculptures—they're great!"

70
00:04:24.485 --> 00:04:24.985
Ally said.

71
00:04:25.005 --> 00:04:27.868
"Thanks," the artist replied.

72
00:04:28.564 --> 00:04:30.446
"I still have one more piece to make.

73
00:04:30.886 --> 00:04:34.129
I'm looking for something with a real wow factor."

74
00:04:34.149 --> 00:04:38.472
"There are some interesting things in the park," Ally said.

75
00:04:38.492 --> 00:04:43.216
"The bandshell, the murals, even the trees are inspiring!"

76
00:04:44.057 --> 00:04:44.937
The artist smiled.

77
00:04:44.957 --> 00:04:47.560
"Thanks. I'm Sarah by the way.

78
00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.002
Oh, and I'll have the Space Cakes, please."

79
00:04:51.022 --> 00:04:54.345
"One order of pancakes coming up!"

80
00:04:56.206 --> 00:04:59.289
As Ally went to put in Sarah's order, she had another inspiration.

81
00:04:59.309 --> 00:05:03.813
"I know what Mateo should do for Bethany's surprise!

82
00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:05.374
I can't wait to tell him!"

83
00:05:09.858 --> 00:05:11.879
Ally headed home from her shift in a good mood.

84
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:16.683
Even though last night's dream had made her miss home, she had a lot to be thankful for

85
00:05:16.743 --> 00:05:17.284
here on Earth.

86
00:05:18.905 --> 00:05:22.088
"Today I helped both Ray and Sarah solve problems.

87
00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.962
By the time I get back to Astralia, I'm going to have a long list of good deeds,"

88
00:05:28.322 --> 00:05:28.862
Ally thought.

89
00:05:28.882 --> 00:05:33.723
"I'll ask Alpha to keep a log for me!"

90
00:05:40.505 --> 00:05:43.966
Ally stopped near the trees and held up her meld medallion to reveal her pod.

91
00:05:44.266 --> 00:05:46.167
But to her surprise, nothing happened.

92
00:05:47.047 --> 00:05:49.768
She held it up again, but still the pod didn't appear.

93
00:05:54.188 --> 00:05:54.369
"Oh no!"

94
00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:55.012
Ally gasped.

95
00:05:55.816 --> 00:05:57.083
Her pod had vanished!
